  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a list of non-negative integers `nums`, arrange them such that they form the largest number and output it.\n\nSince the result may be very large, so you need to output a string instead of an integer.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [10,2]\nOutput: \"210\"\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [3,30,34,5,9]\nOutput: \"9534330\"\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 100`\n* `0 <= nums[i] <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
